  ⚠ jest(prefer-expect-assertions): Every test should have either `e.assertions(<number of assertions>)` or `e.hasAssertions()` as its first expression.
   ╭─[prefer_expect_assertions.tsx:1:41]
 1 │ import { expect as e } from 'bun:test'; it("it1", () => {})
   ·                                         ───────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Add `e.hasAssertions()` or `e.assertions(<number>)` as the first statement in the test.

  ⚠ jest(prefer-expect-assertions): Every test should have either `expect.assertions(<number of assertions>)` or `expect.hasAssertions()` as its first expression.
   ╭─[prefer_expect_assertions.tsx:1:46]
 1 │ import { expect as e } from '@jest/globals'; it("it1", () => {})
   ·                                              ───────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Add `expect.hasAssertions()` or `expect.assertions(<number>)` as the first statement in the test.
